{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"40ad0a99-3d96-45a3-8998-c0b8bfdcb971","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The nightly launchd job was silent because:\n\n1. **Prompt not passed via stdin** – `claude` awaited input and failed.  \n2. **Assigning to the read‑only `status` variable** in a Zsh script killed the script before the failure notifier could run.  \n3. **Missing `USER` environment variable** in the launchd plist prevented the head‑less CLI from accessing the keychain.\n\nAll three issues have been fixed:\n\n* Prompt is piped to `claude`.  \n* Exit code is stored in a regular variable (`rc`).  \n* `USER` is defined in the plist’s `\u003cEnvironmentVariables\u003e`.\n\nThe detailed reasoning and which parts of the colleague’s note were applied are documented in **[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/40ad0a99-3d96-45a3-8998-c0b8bfdcb971/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":32.178092,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":20344,"output_tokens":3006,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":104320,"total_tokens":23350}}}
